      <groundspeak:encoded_hints>FGL FLOWERBED N END 14 ST BRDG

FLUSH W/GRD, IN CITY OF CALGARY FLOWER BED AT NORTH END OF 14 STREET BRIDGE.
elevation 1054.3m. </groundspeak:encoded_hints>
      <groundspeak:logs>
        <groundspeak:log id="1378446229">
          <groundspeak:date>2026-08-13T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="25790230">MaybeSunshine</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP368 Kensington [FOUND]&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I drive past here on 14th almost daily, but today I was actually heading west on Memorial with the time window and vehicle to make a quick stop in a permit zone without worrying. No issues with the find; I didn’t have any tools but it’s in the obvious hole. Quite the interesting spot for a cap.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="684128632">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-05-06T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="12442378">mikefromcanmore</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP368 Kensington.  Took a while to find a place to park and then had to dodge some traffic to get to the correct side of the road.  Discovered there was a tunnel on the way back which simplified matters.  All was quiet at GZ.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="682890337">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-05-01T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="4883787">Kottbullar</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP368 Kensington&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I wanted to take advantage of the nice weather and go out for sone brass caps. &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Had to go under 14th St to get back to the car and had to endure the unwanted attention of a drinking and smoking guy on the ground. Should probably have taken a different route, but lots of people out and about. &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;TFTBC!&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
